  "hindi": "हम तुम्हारी शाखाएँ हैं, हे इन्द्र; हमें भली-भाँति जानो। पुरस्कार की इच्छा करने वाले के समान हम रथ को आगे लाते हैं — स्तुति के इच्छुक, विचार से दीप्त होते हुए, तुम जैसे मनुष्यों से अनुग्रह पाने की कामना करते हुए।",
  "english": "We are your branches, Indra; take good note of us. We bring forward, like one eager for the prize his chariot, eager to praise, shining with thought, desiring favour from men such as you.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "vayāḥ taken as 'branches' (nom. pl. of vayā); the alternative 'vigour, sustenance' (vayas) is not excluded. The object of pra bharāmahe is not stated (the comparison 'like a prize-seeker a chariot' suggests praise or the like); the translation leaves it unstated. iyakṣantaḥ is a desiderative participle (root uncertain, 'desiring to reach/obtain'); the construction tvāvato nṝn with sumnam is unclear: 'favour from men such as you' is the most natural rendering, but 'seeking men such as you for favour' is possible. Lines 1a-1b are one sentence.",
  "confidence": "low",
  "type": "verse",
  "line_ids": [
   "002.020.1a",
   "002.020.1b"
  ],
  "lines_deva": [
   "व॒यं ते॒ वय॑ इन्द्र वि॒द्धि षु ण॒: प्र भ॑रामहे वाज॒युर्न रथ॑म्",
   "वि॒प॒न्यवो॒ दीध्य॑तो मनी॒षा सु॒म्नमिय॑क्षन्त॒स्त्वाव॑तो॒ नॄन्"
