  "hindi": "हे इन्द्र, तुम अपनी सहायता से हम लोगों के, तुम्हारी कामना करने वाले जनों के रक्षक हो। तुम दानी के स्वामी और रक्षक हो, जो सच्चे चिन्तन वाला होकर तुम्हारे पास पहुँचता है।",
  "english": "You, Indra, with your own help, are the protector of us, of the people who long for you. You are the lord and protector of the giver, who, true in thought, draws near to you.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "tvābhiḥ ūtī is obscure: taken as 'with your own help'; the grammar of tvābhiḥ is uncertain (inst. pl. of a possessive), so the sense rests on context. na is taken as 'us' (with janān in apposition); 'our' is also possible. abhiṣṭi-pā 'protector' (literally a guardian who protects from the front or against attack) is rendered plainly. inaḥ 'lord' and varūtā 'protector' taken as two predicates of tvam. itthādhīḥ analysed as ittha 'truly' + dhī 'thought'.",
  "confidence": "low",
  "type": "verse",
