  "hindi": "वह युवा, बहुत बुलाया गया इन्द्र हमारा मित्र और कल्याणकारी होकर मनुष्यों का रक्षक हो — जो अपनी सहायता से स्तुति करने वाले को, श्रम करने वाले को, पकाने वाले को और स्तवन करने वाले को आगे ले चले।",
  "english": "May that young Indra, the much invoked, be our kind friend and the protector of men, he who with his help leads forward the one who recites, the one who toils, the one who cooks and the one who praises.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "praṇeṣat is taken as pra-√nī, aorist subjunctive. ūtī is placed with the verb ('with help'); it could also go with the participles. śaśamāna 'toiling' (√śam 'exert oneself'); pacantam 'cooking' (the object cooked is not stated).",
