  "hindi": "उस इन्द्र की मैं स्तुति करता हूँ, उसी का मैं गान करता हूँ, जिसमें पूर्वकाल में वे बलवान् हुए और प्रबल रहे। वह आकर, ब्रह्म रचने की इच्छा करने वाले नये मनुष्य की धन की कामना पूर्ण करे।",
  "english": "Him, Indra, I praise; him I extol, in whom of old they grew strong and prevailed. May he, coming, fulfil the wish for wealth of the new man who seeks to make prayers.",
  "text_flags": [],
  "notes": "Uncertain points: śāśaduḥ taken as perfect of √śad 'prevail' (the meaning is not secure); the subject of vāvṛdhuḥ (unstated 'they') is left general. vasvaḥ kāmam: vasu 'wealth' (literally good thing); vasvaḥ could be taken with kāmam as 'wish for wealth'. brahmaṇyataḥ from brahmaṇyant 'wishing to make prayer/hymn' (brahman). āyu 'man, living being'; nūtanasya āyoḥ 'of the new man'. gṛṇīṣe is a 1 sg. use here.",
